  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provide life-saving services for children and families on the move in Darien Gap - Panama</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide life-saving services to the most vulnerable migrant children and families in transit at the border between Colombia and Panama, specifically in the Darien Province and Comarca Embera Wounaan. This UNICEF project deploys capacities to respond to and monitor the situation of children and conducts services of Water, Sanitation and Hygiene, Child Protection, and Gender-Based Violence Prevention. The provision of sanitation and hygiene services is critical in allowing for mitigating the impact of migratory transit and reduces the risks of exposure to vectors. The project provides life-saving assistance to 90,445 individuals, including 39,095 men, 19,793 women, 31,693 children, and including 470 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
